# Migrating a flat Pulumi TS program to `ComponentResource` — zero replacements

The whole trick is one fact:

> A resource's **URN** is `urn:pulumi:<stack>::<project>::<parent-type-chain>$<type>::<name>`.
> Re-parenting a resource under a `ComponentResource` changes the *type chain* portion, so Pulumi's engine sees the old URN as deleted and a new URN as created → **delete + create** (data loss on RDS/S3).

`aliases` tells the engine "this new URN is the same resource that used to live at that old URN". For the flat→component migration the old parent was the **stack root**, so every re-parented resource needs:

```ts
{ aliases: [{ noParent: true }] }
```

and, if you also changed its logical name, `{ noParent: true, name: "old-name" }`.

Below: the *before* program, the *after* program, the alias plumbing, stack configs, and the verification procedure.

---

## 0. Repo layout (after)

```
.
├── Pulumi.yaml
├── Pulumi.dev.yaml
├── Pulumi.prod.yaml
├── index.ts
├── config.ts
└── components/
    ├── alias.ts
    ├── storage.ts
    ├── database.ts
    ├── cluster.ts
    ├── identity.ts
    ├── edge.ts
    └── webapp.ts
```

---

## 1. Before — the flat program (`index.ts`, the thing being migrated)

This is what is already deployed in `dev` and `prod`. Names here are the **contract** — they must be preserved or aliased.

```ts
// index.ts  (BEFORE — for reference only)
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as eks from "@pulumi/eks";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";

const cfg = new pulumi.Config();
const env = pulumi.getStack();

const assets = new aws.s3.Bucket("assets", { /* ... */ });
const assetsVersioning = new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2("assets-versioning", { /* ... */ });
const assetsSse = new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2("assets-sse", { /* ... */ });
const assetsPab = new aws.s3.BucketPublicAccessBlock("assets-pab", { /* ... */ });

const dbSubnets = new aws.rds.SubnetGroup("db-subnets", { /* ... */ });
const dbSg = new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup("db-sg", { /* ... */ });
const db = new aws.rds.Instance("db", { /* ... */ });

const svcUser = new aws.iam.User("svc-user", { /* ... */ });
const svcRole = new aws.iam.Role("svc-role", { /* ... */ });

const cluster = new eks.Cluster("cluster", { /* ... */ });

const cert = new aws.acm.Certificate("cert", { /* ... */ });
const cdn = new aws.cloudfront.Distribution("cdn", { /* ... */ });
```

Key point: the **logical names** (`assets`, `db`, `cluster`, `svc-role`, …) are the second half of the URN. Keep them byte-identical inside the components and you only ever have to alias the parent.

---

## 2. The alias helper

```ts
// components/alias.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";

/**
 * Alias for a resource that used to be declared at the top level of the
 * program (i.e. parented to the implicit stack resource) and is now a
 * child of a ComponentResource.
 *
 * `noParent: true` is the explicit way to say "old URN had no parent
 * component" — it is NOT the same as omitting `parent`, which means
 * "unchanged".
 *
 * Pass `oldName` only if the logical name also changed.
 */
export function fromRoot(oldName?: string): pulumi.Alias[] {
    return [oldName ? { noParent: true, name: oldName } : { noParent: true }];
}

/**
 * Escape hatch: alias by literal URN. Use when the project name, stack
 * name, or resource *type* changed too (e.g. aws.s3.Bucket ->
 * aws.s3.BucketV2), where the structured Alias form can't express it.
 */
export function fromUrn(urn: string): pulumi.Alias[] {
    return [{ urn } as pulumi.Alias];
}
```

> **Aliases are inherited.** A child of a component automatically gets aliases derived from its parent's aliases. That means if you later *rename or re-type the component itself*, you do **not** re-alias every child. It does not help for this migration, because the component is brand new — hence the per-child `fromRoot()`.

---

## 3. Typed config

```ts
// config.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";

export interface EnvSpec {
    env: "dev" | "prod";
    region: string;
    nodeCount: number;
    nodeInstanceType: string;
    dbInstanceClass: string;
    dbMultiAz: boolean;
    dbEncrypted: boolean;
    replicaRegion?: string;          // prod only: cross-region replication
    domainName: string;
    hostedZoneId: string;
    oidcProviderArn?: string;        // prod: OIDC trust for the service role
    oidcSubject?: string;
    dbPassword: pulumi.Output<string>;   // secret
}

export function loadConfig(): EnvSpec {
    const c = new pulumi.Config();
    const env = pulumi.getStack() as "dev" | "prod";
    return {
        env,
        region: c.require("region"),
        nodeCount: c.requireNumber("nodeCount"),
        nodeInstanceType: c.require("nodeInstanceType"),
        dbInstanceClass: c.require("dbInstanceClass"),
        dbMultiAz: c.requireBoolean("dbMultiAz"),
        dbEncrypted: c.requireBoolean("dbEncrypted"),
        replicaRegion: c.get("replicaRegion"),
        domainName: c.require("domainName"),
        hostedZoneId: c.require("hostedZoneId"),
        oidcProviderArn: c.get("oidcProviderArn"),
        oidcSubject: c.get("oidcSubject"),
        dbPassword: c.requireSecret("dbPassword"),
    };
}
```

### `Pulumi.dev.yaml`

```yaml
config:
  aws:region: us-east-1
  webapp:region: us-east-1
  webapp:nodeCount: "2"
  webapp:nodeInstanceType: t3.medium
  webapp:dbInstanceClass: db.t3.micro
  webapp:dbMultiAz: "false"
  webapp:dbEncrypted: "false"
  webapp:domainName: dev.example.com
  webapp:hostedZoneId: Z0123456789ABCDEFGHIJ
  webapp:dbPassword:
    secure: AAABANJ...           # `pulumi config set --secret dbPassword`
```

### `Pulumi.prod.yaml`

```yaml
config:
  aws:region: us-east-1
  webapp:region: us-east-1
  webapp:replicaRegion: us-west-2
  webapp:nodeCount: "4"
  webapp:nodeInstanceType: t3.large
  webapp:dbInstanceClass: db.t3.medium
  webapp:dbMultiAz: "true"
  webapp:dbEncrypted: "true"
  webapp:domainName: app.example.com
  webapp:hostedZoneId: Z0123456789ABCDEFGHIJ
  webapp:oidcProviderArn: arn:aws:iam::111122223333:oidc-provider/oidc.eks.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/id/ABC
  webapp:oidcSubject: system:serviceaccount:app:web
  webapp:dbPassword:
    secure: AAABAP7...
```

Secrets are encrypted at rest by the stack's secrets provider (default: Pulumi service KMS envelope; use `pulumi stack change-secrets-provider awskms://...` for a customer-managed key). The ciphertext in `Pulumi.*.yaml` is safe to commit; plaintext never touches Git.

---

## 4. After — the components

### 4.1 Storage

```ts
// components/storage.ts
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { fromRoot } from "./alias";
import { EnvSpec } from "../config";

export class Storage extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly bucket: aws.s3.Bucket;
    public readonly bucketArn: pulumi.Output<string>;

    constructor(name: string, spec: EnvSpec, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("webapp:storage:Storage", name, {}, opts);
        const parent = { parent: this };

        // NOTE: logical name "assets" is unchanged from the flat program.
        this.bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket("assets", {
            forceDestroy: false,
            tags: { Environment: spec.env },
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot(), protect: spec.env === "prod" });

        new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2("assets-versioning", {
            bucket: this.bucket.id,
            versioningConfiguration: { status: "Enabled" },
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2("assets-sse", {
            bucket: this.bucket.id,
            rules: [{
                applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" },
                bucketKeyEnabled: true,
            }],
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        new aws.s3.BucketPublicAccessBlock("assets-pab", {
            bucket: this.bucket.id,
            blockPublicAcls: true,
            blockPublicPolicy: true,
            ignorePublicAcls: true,
            restrictPublicBuckets: true,
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        // ---- prod only: cross-region replication to us-west-2 ----
        if (spec.replicaRegion) {
            const replicaProvider = new aws.Provider("replica-provider",
                { region: spec.replicaRegion as aws.Region },
                { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

            const replica = new aws.s3.Bucket("assets-replica", {
                tags: { Environment: spec.env, Role: "replica" },
            }, { ...parent, provider: replicaProvider, aliases: fromRoot(), protect: true });

            new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2("assets-replica-versioning", {
                bucket: replica.id,
                versioningConfiguration: { status: "Enabled" },
            }, { ...parent, provider: replicaProvider, aliases: fromRoot() });

            new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2("assets-replica-sse", {
                bucket: replica.id,
                rules: [{ applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" } }],
            }, { ...parent, provider: replicaProvider, aliases: fromRoot() });

            const replRole = new aws.iam.Role("assets-replication-role", {
                assumeRolePolicy: JSON.stringify({
                    Version: "2012-10-17",
                    Statement: [{
                        Effect: "Allow",
                        Principal: { Service: "s3.amazonaws.com" },
                        Action: "sts:AssumeRole",
                    }],
                }),
            }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

            new aws.iam.RolePolicy("assets-replication-policy", {
                role: replRole.id,
                policy: pulumi.all([this.bucket.arn, replica.arn]).apply(([src, dst]) =>
                    JSON.stringify({
                        Version: "2012-10-17",
                        Statement: [
                            { Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:GetReplicationConfiguration", "s3:ListBucket"], Resource: [src] },
                            { Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:GetObjectVersionForReplication", "s3:GetObjectVersionAcl", "s3:GetObjectVersionTagging"], Resource: [`${src}/*`] },
                            { Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:ReplicateObject", "s3:ReplicateDelete", "s3:ReplicateTags"], Resource: [`${dst}/*`] },
                        ],
                    })),
            }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

            new aws.s3.BucketReplicationConfig("assets-replication", {
                role: replRole.arn,
                bucket: this.bucket.id,
                rules: [{
                    id: "replicate-all",
                    status: "Enabled",
                    filter: {},
                    deleteMarkerReplication: { status: "Enabled" },
                    destination: { bucket: replica.arn, storageClass: "STANDARD_IA" },
                }],
            }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });
        }

        this.bucketArn = this.bucket.arn;
        this.registerOutputs({ bucket: this.bucket, bucketArn: this.bucketArn });
    }
}
```

### 4.2 Database

```ts
// components/database.ts
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { fromRoot } from "./alias";
import { EnvSpec } from "../config";

export interface DatabaseArgs {
    spec: EnvSpec;
    vpcId: pulumi.Input<string>;
    subnetIds: pulumi.Input<pulumi.Input<string>[]>;
    clientSecurityGroupId: pulumi.Input<string>;
}

export class Database extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly instance: aws.rds.Instance;
    public readonly connectionString: pulumi.Output<string>;   // secret

    constructor(name: string, args: DatabaseArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("webapp:db:Database", name, {}, opts);
        const parent = { parent: this };
        const { spec } = args;

        const subnets = new aws.rds.SubnetGroup("db-subnets", {
            subnetIds: args.subnetIds,
            tags: { Environment: spec.env },
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        const sg = new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup("db-sg", {
            vpcId: args.vpcId,
            description: "Postgres access from application nodes only",
            ingress: [{
                protocol: "tcp", fromPort: 5432, toPort: 5432,
                securityGroups: [args.clientSecurityGroupId],
            }],
            egress: [],
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        this.instance = new aws.rds.Instance("db", {
            engine: "postgres",
            engineVersion: "16.3",
            instanceClass: spec.dbInstanceClass,
            allocatedStorage: spec.env === "prod" ? 100 : 20,
            dbName: "app",
            username: "appadmin",
            password: spec.dbPassword,
            dbSubnetGroupName: subnets.name,
            vpcSecurityGroupIds: [sg.id],
            multiAz: spec.dbMultiAz,
            storageEncrypted: spec.dbEncrypted,
            publiclyAccessible: false,                 // AC #2
            deletionProtection: true,                  // AC #2
            backupRetentionPeriod: spec.env === "prod" ? 30 : 7,  // AC #2 (>= 7)
            skipFinalSnapshot: false,
            finalSnapshotIdentifier: `${spec.env}-app-final`,
            applyImmediately: false,
            tags: { Environment: spec.env },
        }, {
            ...parent,
            aliases: fromRoot(),
            protect: spec.env === "prod",
            // password rotation happens out of band; don't churn on drift
            ignoreChanges: ["password"],
        });

        this.connectionString = pulumi
            .all([this.instance.address, this.instance.port, spec.dbPassword])
            .apply(([host, port, pw]) =>
                pulumi.secret(`postgresql://appadmin:${pw}@${host}:${port}/app?sslmode=require`))
            .apply(o => o);

        this.registerOutputs({ instance: this.instance, connectionString: this.connectionString });
    }
}
```

### 4.3 Cluster

```ts
// components/cluster.ts
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as eks from "@pulumi/eks";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { fromRoot } from "./alias";
import { EnvSpec } from "../config";

export class Cluster extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly cluster: eks.Cluster;
    public readonly kubeconfig: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly nodeSecurityGroupId: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly oidcProviderArn: pulumi.Output<string | undefined>;

    constructor(name: string, spec: EnvSpec, vpc: { vpcId: pulumi.Input<string>;
        publicSubnetIds: pulumi.Input<string[]>; privateSubnetIds: pulumi.Input<string[]> },
        opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("webapp:cluster:Cluster", name, {}, opts);
        const parent = { parent: this };

        this.cluster = new eks.Cluster("cluster", {
            vpcId: vpc.vpcId,
            publicSubnetIds: vpc.publicSubnetIds,
            privateSubnetIds: vpc.privateSubnetIds,
            nodeAssociatePublicIpAddress: false,
            skipDefaultNodeGroup: true,               // managed node group only (AC #5)
            createOidcProvider: true,
            endpointPublicAccess: spec.env !== "prod",
            tags: { Environment: spec.env },
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        new eks.ManagedNodeGroup("cluster-ng", {
            cluster: this.cluster,
            instanceTypes: [spec.nodeInstanceType],
            scalingConfig: {
                desiredSize: spec.nodeCount,
                minSize: spec.nodeCount,
                maxSize: spec.nodeCount * 2,
            },
            nodeRole: this.cluster.instanceRoles.apply(rs => rs[0]),
            subnetIds: vpc.privateSubnetIds,
            labels: { environment: spec.env },
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        this.kubeconfig = pulumi.secret(this.cluster.kubeconfig.apply(k => JSON.stringify(k)));
        this.nodeSecurityGroupId = this.cluster.nodeSecurityGroup.id;
        this.oidcProviderArn = this.cluster.core.oidcProvider!.arn;

        this.registerOutputs({
            kubeconfig: this.kubeconfig,
            nodeSecurityGroupId: this.nodeSecurityGroupId,
        });
    }
}
```

### 4.4 Identity (IAM user + role)

```ts
// components/identity.ts
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { fromRoot } from "./alias";
import { EnvSpec } from "../config";

export interface IdentityArgs {
    spec: EnvSpec;
    bucketArn: pulumi.Input<string>;
    oidcProviderArn?: pulumi.Input<string>;
    oidcSubject?: pulumi.Input<string>;
}

export class Identity extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly roleArn: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly accessKeyId?: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly secretAccessKey?: pulumi.Output<string>;

    constructor(name: string, args: IdentityArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("webapp:iam:Identity", name, {}, opts);
        const parent = { parent: this };
        const { spec } = args;

        // Least-privilege policy: object-level only, no wildcard actions. (AC #4)
        const policyDoc = pulumi.output(args.bucketArn).apply(arn => JSON.stringify({
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [
                { Sid: "ListOwnBucket", Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:ListBucket"], Resource: [arn] },
                {
                    Sid: "RwObjects", Effect: "Allow",
                    Action: ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject", "s3:DeleteObject"],
                    Resource: [`${arn}/*`],
                },
            ],
        }));

        const trust = spec.env === "prod"
            ? pulumi.all([args.oidcProviderArn!, args.oidcSubject!]).apply(([provider, sub]) => {
                const host = provider.split("oidc-provider/")[1];
                return JSON.stringify({
                    Version: "2012-10-17",
                    Statement: [{
                        Effect: "Allow",
                        Principal: { Federated: provider },
                        Action: "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
                        Condition: {
                            StringEquals: {
                                [`${host}:aud`]: "sts.amazonaws.com",
                                [`${host}:sub`]: sub,
                            },
                        },
                    }],
                });
            })
            : pulumi.output(JSON.stringify({
                Version: "2012-10-17",
                Statement: [{
                    Effect: "Allow",
                    Principal: { AWS: `arn:aws:iam::${aws.getCallerIdentityOutput().accountId}:root` },
                    Action: "sts:AssumeRole",
                }],
            }));

        const role = new aws.iam.Role("svc-role", {
            assumeRolePolicy: trust,
            tags: { Environment: spec.env },
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        new aws.iam.RolePolicy("svc-role-policy", {
            role: role.id,
            policy: policyDoc,
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        // Programmatic access only in dev; prod uses OIDC/IRSA exclusively.
        if (spec.env === "dev") {
            const user = new aws.iam.User("svc-user", {
                path: "/service/",
                forceDestroy: true,
            }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

            new aws.iam.UserPolicy("svc-user-policy", {
                user: user.name,
                policy: policyDoc,
            }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

            const key = new aws.iam.AccessKey("svc-user-key", {
                user: user.name,
            }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

            this.accessKeyId = key.id;
            this.secretAccessKey = pulumi.secret(key.secret);
        }

        this.roleArn = role.arn;
        this.registerOutputs({ roleArn: this.roleArn });
    }
}
```

### 4.5 Edge (ACM + CloudFront, HTTPS on 443)

```ts
// components/edge.ts
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { fromRoot } from "./alias";
import { EnvSpec } from "../config";

export class Edge extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly url: pulumi.Output<string>;

    constructor(name: string, spec: EnvSpec, bucket: aws.s3.Bucket,
                opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("webapp:edge:Edge", name, {}, opts);
        const parent = { parent: this };

        // CloudFront requires the cert in us-east-1.
        const usEast1 = new aws.Provider("acm-provider", { region: "us-east-1" },
            { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        const cert = new aws.acm.Certificate("cert", {
            domainName: spec.domainName,
            validationMethod: "DNS",
        }, { ...parent, provider: usEast1, aliases: fromRoot() });

        const validationRecord = new aws.route53.Record("cert-validation", {
            zoneId: spec.hostedZoneId,
            name: cert.domainValidationOptions[0].resourceRecordName,
            type: cert.domainValidationOptions[0].resourceRecordType,
            records: [cert.domainValidationOptions[0].resourceRecordValue],
            ttl: 60,
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        const certValidation = new aws.acm.CertificateValidation("cert-validation-done", {
            certificateArn: cert.arn,
            validationRecordFqdns: [validationRecord.fqdn],
        }, { ...parent, provider: usEast1, aliases: fromRoot() });

        const oac = new aws.cloudfront.OriginAccessControl("cdn-oac", {
            originAccessControlOriginType: "s3",
            signingBehavior: "always",
            signingProtocol: "sigv4",
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        const cdn = new aws.cloudfront.Distribution("cdn", {
            enabled: true,
            aliases: [spec.domainName],
            origins: [{
                originId: "assets",
                domainName: bucket.bucketRegionalDomainName,
                originAccessControlId: oac.id,
            }],
            defaultCacheBehavior: {
                targetOriginId: "assets",
                allowedMethods: ["GET", "HEAD", "OPTIONS"],
                cachedMethods: ["GET", "HEAD"],
                viewerProtocolPolicy: "https-only",   // 443 only, no 80->443 redirect
                compress: true,
                forwardedValues: { queryString: false, cookies: { forward: "none" } },
                minTtl: 0, defaultTtl: 3600, maxTtl: 86400,
            },
            restrictions: { geoRestriction: { restrictionType: "none" } },
            viewerCertificate: {
                acmCertificateArn: certValidation.certificateArn,
                sslSupportMethod: "sni-only",
                minimumProtocolVersion: "TLSv1.2_2021",
            },
            tags: { Environment: spec.env },
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        // Lock the bucket to this distribution only.
        new aws.s3.BucketPolicy("assets-policy", {
            bucket: bucket.id,
            policy: pulumi.all([bucket.arn, cdn.arn]).apply(([b, d]) => JSON.stringify({
                Version: "2012-10-17",
                Statement: [{
                    Effect: "Allow",
                    Principal: { Service: "cloudfront.amazonaws.com" },
                    Action: "s3:GetObject",
                    Resource: `${b}/*`,
                    Condition: { StringEquals: { "AWS:SourceArn": d } },
                }],
            })),
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        new aws.route53.Record("cdn-dns", {
            zoneId: spec.hostedZoneId,
            name: spec.domainName,
            type: "A",
            aliases: [{
                name: cdn.domainName,
                zoneId: cdn.hostedZoneId,
                evaluateTargetHealth: false,
            }],
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        this.url = pulumi.interpolate`https://${spec.domainName}`;
        this.registerOutputs({ url: this.url });
    }
}
```

### 4.6 Top-level component

```ts
// components/webapp.ts
import * as awsx from "@pulumi/awsx";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { fromRoot } from "./alias";
import { EnvSpec } from "../config";
import { Storage } from "./storage";
import { Database } from "./database";
import { Cluster } from "./cluster";
import { Identity } from "./identity";
import { Edge } from "./edge";

export class WebApp extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly url: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly bucketName: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly dbEndpoint: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly dbConnectionString: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly kubeconfig: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly serviceRoleArn: pulumi.Output<string>;

    constructor(name: string, spec: EnvSpec, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("webapp:index:WebApp", name, {}, opts);
        const parent = { parent: this };

        const vpc = new awsx.ec2.Vpc("vpc", {
            numberOfAvailabilityZones: spec.env === "prod" ? 3 : 2,
            natGateways: { strategy: spec.env === "prod" ? "OnePerAz" : "Single" },
            tags: { Environment: spec.env },
        }, { ...parent, aliases: fromRoot() });

        const cluster = new Cluster("cluster", spec, {
            vpcId: vpc.vpcId,
            publicSubnetIds: vpc.publicSubnetIds,
            privateSubnetIds: vpc.privateSubnetIds,
        }, parent);

        const storage = new Storage("storage", spec, parent);

        const database = new Database("database", {
            spec,
            vpcId: vpc.vpcId,
            subnetIds: vpc.privateSubnetIds,
            clientSecurityGroupId: cluster.nodeSecurityGroupId,
        }, parent);

        const identity = new Identity("identity", {
            spec,
            bucketArn: storage.bucketArn,
            oidcProviderArn: spec.oidcProviderArn ?? cluster.oidcProviderArn,
            oidcSubject: spec.oidcSubject,
        }, parent);

        const edge = new Edge("edge", spec, storage.bucket, parent);

        this.url = edge.url;
        this.bucketName = storage.bucket.bucket;
        this.dbEndpoint = database.instance.endpoint;
        this.dbConnectionString = database.connectionString;
        this.kubeconfig = cluster.kubeconfig;
        this.serviceRoleArn = identity.roleArn;

        this.registerOutputs({
            url: this.url,
            bucketName: this.bucketName,
            dbEndpoint: this.dbEndpoint,
            serviceRoleArn: this.serviceRoleArn,
        });
    }
}
```

